From 6ba96984ac8a5f019edd84d7a83c278e6a1d363d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chanyeong Lim <dlacksdud2@snu.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:05:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] qsa_select: the top-k past the register kernel's reach on
 1,024 threads with a histogram per warp (CUDA) - 9-12x at 262K-524K cells, a
 243K-token prompt +26% on an RTX 3060

On CUDA the register kernel holds 33,792 blocks (~135K cells). Past it qsa_block_topk took the original kernel:
256 threads, each reading its own stretch of the scores on all six passes, one shared histogram updated with
atomics. The dispatch follows the capacity (--max-context), so with a context past ~135K that was every prompt
batch and every decode window on a card without the sm_75 active-bound dispatch (#512), whatever the prompt's
length, and on sm_75 every prompt batch past 33,792 blocks and every decode window.

block_topk_wide_kernel is the register kernel's layout (1,024 threads, a histogram per warp, warp scans) with the
keys read from memory:
- the four radix passes: thread t reads blocks t, t + 1024, ... - a histogram has no order, so a warp reads 32
  neighbours at a time;
- the count and the output: warp w holds `per` rows of 32 consecutive blocks, and the cells are written in the
  order (warp, row, lane); a row without a selected block is skipped.
The selection rule is the original kernel's (radix threshold, ties to the lowest index, cells ascending): identical
ids. One launch per call, no scratch memory, no capacity limit.

Dispatch (CUDA; HIP is unchanged and does not compile the kernel): where the blocks do not fit the registers the
new kernel, except a call that names fewer than 4,608 blocks (a prompt batch below ~18K cells), which keeps the
original kernel: its fixed cost is lower there. A decode window (no block count) takes the new kernel at any
context. The register kernel's range, the sm_75 active-bound dispatch and the sm_90+ cluster path are unchanged.
STRATA_TOPK_OLD=1 keeps the original kernel, as before.

qsa_topk_parity (new, with the kernel parity tests): the dispatched top-k against qsa_block_topk_ref on both sides
of the register kernel's reach, at short contexts under a long capacity and up to 524,288 cells, called as decode
and as the prompt path call it, with continuous scores, 64 score levels and equal scores.

RTX 3060 12 GB (sm_86), 256 queries with their block count under a 262,144-cell capacity (524,288 for the last
two), original -> dispatched:
  16K cells    0.199 -> 0.199 ms (the original kernel)
  32K          0.845 -> 0.328
  131K         4.70  -> 0.97
  262K        16.09  -> 1.71
  393K        26.02  -> 2.49
  524K        37.53  -> 3.24
4 queries without a count (a decode window): 0.031 -> 0.028 ms at 8K, 0.176 -> 0.083 at 131K, 0.309 -> 0.127 at
262K.

IQ3_XXS on that card (--resident-experts, --max-context 262144, --kv int8 --kv-resident 32768),
tools/needle_bench.py, STRATA_TOPK_OLD=1 against the default: tok/s of the prompt, and the prompt path's selection
phase (STRATA_PREFILL_TIMING):
  16,471 tokens    1004.5, 1016.2 ->  989.0, 1013.6       195 ->    195 ms
  31,970           1043.3, 1055.5 -> 1060.1, 1060.5       900 ->    731
  61,333            932.9         -> 1013.8             4,061 ->  2,428
  122,755           904.7,  904.2 ->  992.7,  989.6    20,019 ->  9,034
  185,729           819.7         ->  954.7            50,055 -> 20,761
  243,176           743.3         ->  933.7            96,326 -> 35,544
The needles are found in every run.

